From 48e79b39c5c069f682bbf5f3e68afd37618a3a1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:44:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 38/42] Autoroute tool: KiCadRoutingTools and Freerouting, with
 fan-out, planes and optimize

Route > Autoroute... is now a tool with a router choice (KiCadRoutingTools,
run in a process of its own with the bundled Python, or Freerouting) and
tabs to route every or chosen nets (optionally as a bus, or only between
chosen parts, on chosen layers), fan out parts, pour planes and optimize
routed nets.  A run is modal, so the board cannot be edited under the
router; it shows its steps, progress and the router's output, can be
paused, resumed and stopped, and is one undo step kept or discarded at the
end.  The MCP tools pcb_autoroute, pcb_autoroute_status and
pcb_autoroute_control drive the same tool.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
